sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client
  participant API as Control API
  participant CDB as control schema
  participant CDC as Debezium Connect
  participant Kafka
  participant Orch as Orchestrator
  participant WDB as workflow schema
  participant Provider as Provider gRPC
  participant Projection as projection schema

  Client->>API: POST instance + JWT + idempotency key + traceparent
  API->>API: HTTP span + authorization + command-accept span
  API->>CDB: One transaction: intent, operation, lease, audit, outbox
  Note over API,CDB: Outbox stores the versioned envelope and serialized W3C context.
  CDB-->>API: Commit
  API-->>Client: 202 Accepted + operation ID

  CDC->>CDB: Read committed WAL change
  CDC->>CDC: db-log-write + outbox-relay spans
  CDC-)Kafka: Publish keyed command with W3C headers
  Kafka-)Orch: At-least-once delivery + broker append timestamp
  Orch->>Orch: Restore context + consumer span + bounded handler retries
  Orch->>WDB: Commit inbox receipt and initial workflow
  Orch->>Kafka: Commit offset only after database commit

  loop One leased and fenced transition per claim
    Orch->>WDB: Claim checkpoint and restore persisted parent context
    Orch->>Orch: workflow-stage span
    Orch->>Provider: Provider gRPC with stable request ID
    Provider-->>Orch: Task, result, or observed state
    Orch->>WDB: Commit checkpoint and workflow outbox event
  end

  CDC->>WDB: Read committed workflow outbox
  CDC-)Kafka: Publish progress or terminal fact
  Kafka-)API: Projection consumer delivery
  API->>Projection: Apply read model and receipt atomically
  API->>Kafka: Commit offset

  opt Governed dead-letter replay
    Kafka-)Orch: Replay request with operator attribution
    Orch->>WDB: Commit replay decision + resolution outbox fact
    Note over Orch,WDB: The Orchestrator never updates the control schema.
    CDC->>WDB: Read committed replay resolution
    CDC-)Kafka: Publish provisioning.replay.resolved
    Kafka-)API: Deliver replay resolution fact
    API->>CDB: Update replay request in owner transaction
    API->>Projection: Update admin projection + receipt atomically
    API->>Kafka: Commit offset
  end

  Client->>API: GET operation and instance
  API->>Projection: Read project-scoped documents
  Projection-->>API: succeeded + active
  API-->>Client: Desired and observed state

  Note over API,Provider: One trace ID crosses HTTP, PostgreSQL, Debezium, Kafka, workflow restart, and gRPC.
